{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Keys","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey"],"title":"Keys"},{"anchor":"Protocol","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore"],"title":"Protocol"},{"anchor":"Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore"],"title":"Implementations"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"],["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist scalar preferences like theme, sort order, or last-seen version — testably, with type-safe keys."}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Reference","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"],"title":"Reference"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup","title":"KeyValueStore"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","isActive":true},{"text":" is a small protocol for one-shot scalar values that don’t fit","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"text":" model. Three implementations ship:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — production, backed by any ","type":"text"},{"code":"UserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" suite","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — production, backed by the system Keychain (survives reinstall)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — tests, dictionary-backed, reference semantics","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Inject through your ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Environment"},{"text":", hydrate state at startup, and write from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"effects. Reducers stay pure.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["public protocol KeyValueStore: Sendable {","    func value<Value>(_ key: KVKey<Value>) -> Value?","    func setValue<Value>(_ value: Value?, for key: KVKey<Value>)","    func removeValue<Value>(for key: KVKey<Value>)","    func contains<Value>(_ key: KVKey<Value>) -> Bool","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"All values are JSON-encoded as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data"},{"text":". Reads and writes go through ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","isActive":true},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which pairs a backing-store name with its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" value type at compile time.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"When-to-Use-What","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"When to Use What"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Need","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Collection of identifiable entities (decks, cards, sessions)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Scalar preference (theme, sort order, last-seen version)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" (UserDefaults)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Anonymous device identity that must survive reinstall","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" (Keychain)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Last-known-good entitlement cache (offline pro gate)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" (Keychain) — backs ","type":"text"},{"code":"ResilientPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntityStore"},{"text":" is for many-of-a-kind data with change tracking and batched","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyValueStore"},{"text":" is for one-of-a-kind values that you read once at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"startup and overwrite on change.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"UserDefaults-vs-Keychain","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"UserDefaults vs Keychain"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","isActive":true}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Survives reinstall?","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Yes (this-device-only by default)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Backup \/ device migration","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Included","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Excluded with default accessibility","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Throughput","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Fast (in-memory cache)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Slower (system call)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Visible to other apps?","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No (per app\/group)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Optionally (App Groups via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessGroup:"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Best for","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Theme, sort order, feature toggles, last-seen version","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Anonymous device ID, opaque tokens, last-known-good entitlement","type":"text"}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Keychain costs more per access — hydrate once at launch and observe state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"afterward, never read inside a reducer.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Prefer the Keychain for anything a user could gain by forging it. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"last-known-good entitlement cache is the clearest case: it grants pro offline,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UserDefaults"},{"text":" plist (editable directly or via a doctored-backup restore)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lets a spoofed value unlock the app. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ResilientPaywallService"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"persists that cache through an injected ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyValueStore"},{"text":", so back it with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Keychain.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"macOS-sandbox--entitlements","text":"macOS sandbox & entitlements","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeychainKeyValueStore"},{"text":" uses the data-protection keychain, so it never raises","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a user prompt — no “Always Allow \/ Deny” dialog, no locked-keychain prompt, no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Touch ID \/ Face ID challenge.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"tip","name":"Tip","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"sandboxed","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" macOS app still needs a keychain entitlement, even when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not sharing items across an access group. Xcode supplies an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"application-identifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" automatically for provisioning-profile–signed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"builds; otherwise add an explicit "},{"code":"keychain-access-groups","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entry:"}]},{"code":["<key>keychain-access-groups<\/key>","<array>","    <string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.example.myapp<\/string>","<\/array>"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"xml"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Without it, the first ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setValue"},{"text":" fails with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"errSecMissingEntitlement"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OSStatus"},{"text":" −34018). This is a build\/signing condition, not a runtime","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"prompt. iOS \/ iPadOS \/ tvOS \/ watchOS need no extra entitlement.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Encryption, accessibility, iCloud-sync exclusion, and backup exclusion are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identical whichever entitlement you use — the access group only controls","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which of your own apps"}]},{"text":" can read an item, never third parties or the cloud.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"For a private device ID, in order of strictness:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Most private:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" profile-signed build + "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessGroup: nil"},{"text":", relying on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"implicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application-identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" group. No other app — even same-team —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be entitled to it. Mirrors the iOS default; zero sharing surface."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Practically equivalent:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"keychain-access-groups"},{"type":"text","text":" array whose only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entry is the team-prefixed bundle id (the snippet above). Use when a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"profile-signed build isn’t available (unsigned local \/ CI dev). Only delta:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a same-team app you sign could also declare that string."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Intentional sharing only:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" a shared group string. The "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"first","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"becomes the default group for new items — never put a shared group first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for private data."}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Device-Identity-Pattern","text":"Device-Identity Pattern","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The original motivation for "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" was apps without user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"auth that still want stable identity for analytics. Mint a UUID once with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/deviceIdentity(key:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" helper, hydrate into "},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" at launch,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and feed it to "},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"same","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"deviceID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is also the stable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"feature-flag bucketing identity (the plugin’s "},{"code":"deviceIDKeyPath","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), so analytics"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and A\/B exposure share one identity:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ `KVKey.deviceID` and `deviceIdentity()` ship with Swidux.","","\/\/ In Store.configured(), before constructing the store:","let kv = KeychainKeyValueStore(service: \"com.example.myapp\")","let deviceID = kv.deviceIdentity()   \/\/ reads, or mints-and-persists, a stable UUID","","let initialState = AppState(deviceID: deviceID, \/* … *\/)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Then in the analytics plugin wiring:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["AnalyticsPlugin(","    service: analytics,","    identity: AnalyticsIdentity(userID: \\.deviceID, properties: { _ in [:] }),","    \/\/ …",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The closure-based "},{"code":"userID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" keypath runs on every dispatch, so the value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"must","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" live in state — never call into the Keychain from the closure. Hydrate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once; observe state."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Type-safe-Keys","text":"Type-safe Keys","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare each key once on "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" so the value type travels with the name —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no magic strings at call sites:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["extension KVKey where Value == Theme {","    static let theme = KVKey<Theme>(\"theme\")","}","","extension KVKey where Value == SortOrder {","    static let sortOrder = KVKey<SortOrder>(\"sortOrder\")","}","","extension KVKey where Value == String {","    static let lastSeenVersion = KVKey<String>(\"lastSeenVersion\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Then read and write through static-member literals. The compiler enforces"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that the value type matches what you declared:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let theme = store.value(.theme) ?? .system            \/\/ Theme?","store.setValue(theme, for: .theme)","store.setValue(.alphabetical, for: .sortOrder)","store.removeValue(for: .lastSeenVersion)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A typo or wrong type produces a compile error, not a silent miss at runtime."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Centralizing keys on "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" also gives you autocomplete and a single place"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to audit your preference surface."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Wiring","text":"Wiring","type":"heading"},{"level":3,"anchor":"1-Add-to-your-environment","text":"1. Add to your environment","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct AppEnvironment: Sendable {","    var keyValue: any KeyValueStore","","    static func live() -> AppEnvironment {","        AppEnvironment(keyValue: UserDefaultsKeyValueStore())","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"2-Hydrate-at-startup","text":"2. Hydrate at startup","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read once into the initial state — never read mid-cycle from a reducer."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["extension AppState {","    static func hydrated(from store: any KeyValueStore) -> AppState {","        AppState(","            theme: store.value(.theme) ?? .system,","            sortOrder: store.value(.sortOrder) ?? .alphabetical,","            lastSeenVersion: store.value(.lastSeenVersion)","        )","    }","}","","let env = AppEnvironment.live()","let store = AppStore.configured(state: .hydrated(from: env.keyValue), environment: env)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"3-Write-from-an-effect","text":"3. Write from an effect","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mutate state in the reducer, return an effect that writes the value:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["case .themeChanged(let theme):","    state.theme = theme","    return { @Sendable _ in","        environment.keyValue.setValue(theme, for: .theme)","    }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No "},{"code":"try?","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", no "},{"code":"do\/catch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/setValue(_:for:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" does not throw —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder errors are programmer mistakes (e.g. "},{"code":"Float.nan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), so the store logs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them and triggers "},{"code":"assertionFailure","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in DEBUG instead of forcing every effect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to handle an "},{"code":"Error","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" it can’t act on."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Testing","text":"Testing","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inject "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and assert against the same instance:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Test","@MainActor","func themeChangePersists() async throws {","    let prefs = InMemoryKeyValueStore()","    let env = AppEnvironment(keyValue: prefs)","    let store = AppStore.configured(state: AppState(), environment: env)","","    try await confirmation(expectedCount: 1) { confirm in","        store.send(.themeChanged(.dark))","","        for _ in 0..<50 {","            if prefs.value(.theme) == .dark {","                confirm()","                break","            }","            try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(10))","        }","    }","","    \/\/ Simulate a relaunch.","    let rehydrated = AppState.hydrated(from: prefs)","    #expect(rehydrated.theme == .dark)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tests touching real "},{"code":"UserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" should use a fresh per-test suite and tear"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it down explicitly:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let suiteName = \"myapp.tests.\\(UUID().uuidString)\"","let defaults = UserDefaults(suiteName: suiteName)!","defer { defaults.removePersistentDomain(forName: suiteName) }","","let store = UserDefaultsKeyValueStore(suite: defaults)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Reads-Are-For-Hydration","text":"Reads Are For Hydration","type":"heading"},{"style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reading from ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" mid-cycle (inside a reducer) is an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anti-pattern. Reducers must be pure and synchronous; reads happen once at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"text":" construction. After hydration, the value lives in state and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"downstream code observes state, not the store.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"UserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" itself is thread-safe, but a reducer reading while an effect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes creates ordering ambiguity. Hydrate, observe state, write through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"effects — that’s the discipline."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Failure-Modes","text":"Failure Modes","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Missing key","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/value(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":". Provide a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default at the call site."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Decode failure","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" and logs through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os.Logger"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(subsystem "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"swidux\""},{"type":"text","text":", category "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"kvstore\""},{"type":"text","text":"). On startup, behaves identically"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to first launch."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Encode failure","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — logged at the same subsystem\/category, then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assertionFailure"},{"type":"text","text":" fires in DEBUG so the bug surfaces during development."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Production builds log and continue; the in-memory state is unchanged. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API does not throw — there is no useful runtime recovery from inside an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"effect, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try?"},{"type":"text","text":" would just hide the problem."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":2,"anchor":"AppStorage-Interop","text":"@AppStorage Interop","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There is none, by design. "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" writes JSON-encoded"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" blobs. SwiftUI’s "},{"code":"@AppStorage","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" only observes native primitive types"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"Bool","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"URL","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", raw "},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). Two parallel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observation channels — Swidux state and "},{"code":"@AppStorage","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — would drift."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux state is the source of truth. Read once at hydration, then observe"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state through the store."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Schema-Migration","text":"Schema Migration","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Out of scope for "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". If a "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" shape changes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incompatibly, declare a new versioned key:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ before:","extension KVKey where Value == Theme {","    static let theme = KVKey<Theme>(\"theme\")","}","\/\/ after a breaking shape change:","extension KVKey where Value == Theme {","    static let theme = KVKey<Theme>(\"theme.v2\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Old keys can be cleaned up at startup with "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/removeValue(for:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(declare a tombstone "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" of any value type — only the name is read)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStore/deviceIdentity(key:)":{"kind